From 3d8f02918cf3a88f1a01b6cd426a676dfca8a81e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Venkatesh Perumal <venper@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 11:26:54 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: msi: Add workaround to restore MSI data during pci msi
 resume

MSI data associated with the MHI device is overwritten with "0"
during the MSI restore flow:
_pci_restore_msi_state->arch_restore_msi_irqs
This cause the MHIInterfcae to fail after resume due to incorrect
MSI configuration.

Add a workaround to restore the MSI data during resume and
ensure the proper MHI interrupt functionality.

Signed-off-by: Venkatesh Perumal <venper@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
 drivers/pci/msi/msi.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/msi/msi.c b/drivers/pci/msi/msi.c
index 8b8848788618..65a5485c39d0 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/msi/msi.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/msi/msi.c
@@ -516,6 +516,10 @@ void __pci_restore_msi_state(struct pci_dev *dev)
 
 	entry = irq_get_msi_desc(dev->irq);
 
+	printk("NXP-IMX95-RC: %s: IRQ %d Before updated msg data is %d\n", __func__, entry->irq, entry->msg.data);
+	entry->msg.data = 0x0;
+	printk("NXP-IMX95-RC: %s: IRQ %d After updated msg data is %d\n", __func__, entry->irq, entry->msg.data);
+
 	pci_intx_for_msi(dev, 0);
 	pci_msi_set_enable(dev, 0);
 	if (arch_restore_msi_irqs(dev))
-- 
2.17.1

